        "section": "compile",
        "source_id": "sqlite-3.53.4-docs",
        "start": 339,
        "text": "When compiled with SQLITE_THREADSAFE=2, SQLite can be used in a multithreaded program so long as no two threads attempt to use the same database connection (or any prepared statements derived from that database connection) at the same time.",
        "title": "compile"
      },
      {
        "end": 1132,
        "estimated_tokens": 64,
        "kind": "code_block",
        "page_id": 10,
        "position": 6,
        "record_id": "9123361d84e174851100ff2e",
        "score": 0.5435714285714286,
        "section": "compile",
        "source_id": "sqlite-3.53.4-docs",
        "start": 930,
        "text": "When SQLite has been compiled with SQLITE_THREADSAFE=1 or SQLITE_THREADSAFE=2 then the threading mode can be altered at run-time using the sqlite3_config() interface together with one of these verbs:",
        "title": "compile"
      },
      {
        "end": 823,
        "estimated_tokens": 71,
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "page_id": 10,
        "position": 4,
        "record_id": "9123361d84e174851100ff2e",
        "score": 0.485,
        "section": "compile",
        "source_id": "sqlite-3.53.4-docs",
        "start": 592,
        "text": "To put it another way, SQLITE_THREADSAFE=1 sets the default threading mode to Serialized. SQLITE_THREADSAFE=2 sets the default threading mode to Multi-threaded. And SQLITE_THREADSAFE=0 sets the threading mode to Single-threaded.",
        "title": "compile"
      },
      {
        "end": 349,
        "estimated_tokens": 103,
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "page_id": 14,
        "position": 0,
        "record_id": "9df5eed704858ddff8cccd35",
        "score": 0.4713809391882342,
        "section": "threadsafe",
        "source_id": "sqlite-3.53.4-docs",
        "start": 0,
        "text": "Use the SQLITE_THREADSAFE compile-time parameter to select the threading mode. If no SQLITE_THREADSAFE compile-time parameter is present, then serialized mode is used. This can be made explicit with -DSQLITE_THREADSAFE=1. With -DSQLITE_THREADSAFE=0 the threading mode is single-thread. With -DSQLITE_THREADSAFE=2 the threading mode is multi-thread.",
        "title": "threadsafe"
      },
      {
        "end": 173,
        "estimated_tokens": 59,
        "kind": "paragraph",
        "page_id": 9,
        "position": 0,
        "record_id": "d660299e870f9680794da980",
        "score": 0.4498493254592143,
        "section": "threadsafe",
        "source_id": "sqlite-3.53.4-docs",
        "start": 0,
        "text": "The sqlite3_threadsafe() function returns zero if and only if SQLite was compiled with mutexing code omitted due to the SQLITE_THREADSAFE compile-time option being set to 0.",
        "title": "threadsafe"
      }
    ],
